---
// MultiSourceNerveConvergenceDiagram.astro
// Ultra-clean, focused 3D medical visual of the skull and trigeminal nerve.
// Strictly compliant with the 3 to 4 word title standard: No colons, no ampersands, no dashes.
---

<div class="nerve-convergence-interactive-container tts-ignore" style="margin: 2.25rem 0 2.75rem; background: #070312; border: 1.5px solid #3b1d6e; border-radius: 16px; padding: 1.75rem; box-shadow: 0 16px 45px -10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.8); color: #f8fafc;">
  
  <!-- Header (Strict 3-4 Word Titles) -->
  <div style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #1e1338; padding-bottom: 1rem;">
    <div style="font-size: 0.76rem; font-weight: 800; color: #a855f7; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">
      Cranial Anatomy
    </div>
    <div style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 900; color: #ffffff; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0.45rem;">
      Craniofacial Hardware Wiring
    </div>
    <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; max-width: 820px;">
      A high-fidelity 3D anatomical visualization mapping the full biological path: Cerebral Cortex on top, Trigeminal Ganglion with V2/V3 nerve trunks in the center, and the Oral Cavity with exposed cervical tubules, leaking margins, and pooling acid at the base.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- 3D Anatomical Render - Clean centered image only -->
  <div style="width: 100%; border-radius: 14px; overflow: hidden; background: #030108; border: 1px solid #281447; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; padding: 0.5rem 0;">
    <img 
      src="/trigeminal-v2-v3-nerves-real.jpg" 
      alt="3D medical render of human skull, brain, trigeminal nerve trunks V2 V3, and oral cavity innervation" 
      style="width: 100%; max-width: 820px; height: auto; max-height: 680px; object-fit: contain; object-position: center; display: block; border-radius: 10px; filter: contrast(1.15) brightness(0.98);"
      loading="lazy"
    />
  </div>

</div>
